.95,"rationale":"The bill imposes new policy, reporting, and grievance-procedure obligations on local educational agencies and state education systems."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would require states to ensure that local school districts adopt policies prohibiting bullying and harassment of students based on race, color, national origin, disability, religion, sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and intersex traits). School districts would need to notify students and parents annually about these policies, establish complaint procedures, and publicly report data on bullying incidents. The Department of Education would evaluate anti-bullying programs every two years, and the National Center for Education Statistics would collect nationwide data on these incidents.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"School districts, and children in them. Children, and the adults responsible for them.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"M000687","score":0.05798866766035882},"overlapCount":178},"meaning":{"percentile":41.15791134248304,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.42206171012757976}},{"billId":"119-hr-1106","bioguideId":"T000474","cycle":2026,"score":0.005877079809848965,"matches":[{"industry":"agriculture","donorAmount":14000,"donorShare":0.022108137215732782,"billConfidence":0.55,"contribution":0.00405315848955101},{"industry":"education","donorAmount":5430,"donorShare":0.008574798934387786,"billConfidence":0.5,"contribution":0.0014291331557312976},{"industry":"pharma","donorAmount":1000,"donorShare":0.0015791526582666273,"billConfidence":0.75,"contribution":0.0003947881645666568}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.42206171012757976},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-1106","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"1106","title":"Scientific Integrity Act","introducedDate":"2025-02-06","latestActionDate":"2025-02-06","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on Science, Space, and Technology.","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"T000469","cosponsorCount":136,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1106","industries":[{"industry":"pharma","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Pharmaceutical and biotech companies conduct and rely on federally funded research subject to these integrity requirements."},{"industry":"energy-fossil","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"Federal research on climate, emissions, and energy impacts this sector's regulatory environment and public discourse."},{"industry":"energy-renewable","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"Federal research on energy technologies and climate directly affects this sector's market and policy landscape."},{"industry":"agriculture","confidence":0.55,"rationale":"Agricultural research conducted or funded by USDA and other agencies would be subject to these integrity standards."},{"industry":"education","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"Universities receive federal research funding and would need to comply with integrity policies in their federally supported work."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would require every federal agency that funds, conducts, or oversees scientific research to create and enforce a policy protecting scientific integrity. These policies must ensure that research conclusions are not influenced by political considerations, prohibit suppression or alteration of findings, and allow researchers to share their work. Each agency would need to appoint a Scientific Integrity Officer, establish a complaint process, provide training, and submit its policy to the White House Office of Science and Technology Policy for approval.","classifi